MLLM description: The Australian Terrier is a small, low-set dog with a compact body and sturdy build. Its distinctive physical features include a short, straight coat that can be blue or silver-grey with tan markings on the legs and face, or alternatively sandy or red. The coat is hard and straight, and the ears are either pricked or dropped forward. The tail is docked short.

In terms of size and proportions, the Australian Terrier typically stands about 10 inches tall at the shoulder and weighs between 10-11 pounds. The breed has a sturdy, muscular frame with a strong neck and a deep chest.

Behaviorally, Australian Terriers are known to be alert, independent, and sometimes stubborn. They are often described as feisty and have a high prey drive, which makes them excellent rat catchers. They are also highly intelligent and can be trained to perform various tasks.

Unique identifying traits of the Australian Terrier include its distinctive coat coloration, short and straight coat, and the combination of pricked or dropped forward ears. Additionally, their compact body shape and sturdy build set them apart from other terrier breeds.
